      "gap": "Durrett app. A.1 (p. 458) motivates the cover outer measure before defining measurability: if nu is any measure agreeing with mu on the algebra A, then nu(E) <= nu(union Ai) <= sum mu(Ai) for every cover, so mu*(E) is an upper bound on the measure of E under every such extension, and intuitively the measurable sets are those for which this upper bound is tight. def:p15-cover-outer-measure and the text around it define mu* without this justification, and no route file states that every measure extending the premeasure is dominated by mu* on sigma(A).",
