      "gap": "Durrett p. 3, immediately after Theorem 1.1.4, justifies the interval convention: the choice of closed on the right in (a, b] is dictated by the fact that if bn decreases to b then the intersection of the sets (a, bn] is (a, b], and the semialgebra definition that follows explains the choice of open on the left (the complement of a half-open interval is a finite disjoint union of such intervals). def:p15-stieltjes-intervals, whose subject is these endpoint conventions, fixes I(a, b) = (a, b] without either justification, and no route file states it.",
